@startuml
 title GroupWave — репликация и региональный DR
 left to right direction
 skinparam shadowing false
 skinparam packageStyle rectangle
 skinparam defaultFontSize 12

 cloud "DNS / Traffic Manager\nactive region routing" as DNS
 package "Region A — PRIMARY / active writer" as A {
   rectangle "Application services\nGateway / Message / Chat" as AppA
   database "DynamoDB messages\nPrimary writer" as DDBA
   database "PostgreSQL Multi-AZ\nPrimary + standby" as PGA
   queue "MSK Kafka\nRF=3, min ISR=2" as KafkaA
   database "S3 media bucket\nversioning" as S3A
 }
 package "Region B — DR / warm standby" as B {
   rectangle "Minimum standby apps\nscaled up during DR" as AppB
   database "DynamoDB replica\nwrite disabled until fencing" as DDBB
   database "PostgreSQL async replica" as PGB
   queue "Kafka DR cluster" as KafkaB
   database "S3 replica bucket" as S3B
 }

 DNS --> AppA : normal traffic
 AppA --> DDBA : message write
 AppA --> PGA : users / groups
 AppA --> KafkaA : publish / consume
 AppA --> S3A : media access
 DDBA ..> DDBB : Global Tables / stream replication
 PGA ..> PGB : async WAL / backup replication
 KafkaA ..> KafkaB : cross-region replication
 S3A ..> S3B : S3 CRR
 DNS ..> AppB : switch after DR declared
 AppB --> DDBB : enable writes only after fencing old region
 AppB --> PGB : promote after validation
 AppB --> KafkaB : switch producers/consumers
 AppB --> S3B : use replicated media

 note bottom of A
   Local HA: PostgreSQL Multi-AZ;
   Kafka RF=3; managed DynamoDB durability.
 end note
 note bottom of B
   Secondary region is not an independent active writer in normal operation.
   Incident Commander declares DR; SRE fences Region A before enabling writes here.
 end note
 legend bottom
   Solid = normal request path; dotted = asynchronous replication/failover path.
   RPO targets are limits to test, not a guarantee inferred only from this diagram.
 endlegend
@enduml
